  "worked_solution": "The best deal is the box with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three boxes. To compute the unit price, we divide the price by the total number of ounces.   \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n3.00÷15=0.20\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $A$ is $$0.20.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $B,$ we get\n\n$$\n3.24÷18=0.18\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $B$ is $$0.18.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $C,$ we get\n\n$$\n4.32÷24=0.18\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $C$ is $$0.18$ too.\n\nFrom the above, we see that boxes $B$ and  $C$ have the lowest unit price of $$0.18/\\text{oz}.$ Therefore, boxes $B$ and $C$ offer the best deal.",
